 "title": "Why brands should trust content creators with creative control",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "This creator argues that brands should give content creators full ownership over their scripts, word choice, and direction. By allowing authentic, creator-led storytelling, he claims businesses can see much higher conversion rates compared to standard advertisements.",
 "key_points": [
  "Typical ads have a 3-5% conversion rate.",
  "The creator's own ad campaigns reached a 10% conversion rate.",
  "In one case, 1,100 out of 11,000 users who clicked a link converted into buyers.",
  "In another instance, the Return on Ad Spend (ROAS) was 16, meaning for every 100 rupees spent, the brand made 1600 rupees back.",
  "Allowing creators to control the content ensures it speaks in a language and style that truly resonates with the target audience."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Mohammed Furqan. Text / caption: Consequences of a creator being creative. Transcript: I don't know if you would remember, but I had a collaboration with this project, Rajapushpa Provincia last year. And you know what was the success behind it? When they used my video and ran it as an ad for a bunch of months, and when they came back with the results, usually when you run an ad, there is like 3% or 5% conversion rate, right? But my ad gave them 10% conversion rate, which is for about 11,000 people who may have clicked on the link with the with the video, 1,100 of them converted into potential buyers. The same with cubelillo.com. When I had a collab with them about Rubik's cubes, I was narrating my story around it, and when they ran it as an ad, they came back after a month, and you know what was the result? For every 100 rupees that they spent, they made 16 times back. The ROAS, the return on ad spend was 16 in the ratio. This is what content creation is all about. If you're a brand and you're letting the creator to have the complete ownership of what goes into the script, what words he's using, what's the direction and flow that he's deciding with, on the business front, it will convert. Because the language of the content is speaking directly to the audience that understands in the very language that the creator speaks. Trust content creators. They'll tell you more about how to get creative with the ads. Important text on screen: Dear brands. please listen. What you're looking around me. A WORLD INSIDE A WORLD. It feels like Singapore. Hi my name is Furqan and I can solve this cube in 16 seconds. Their ROAS was between 7-16.",
